# SAUNA alone, a win: the 96 peanuts and 4 corks with no ghost met. The
# ghosts turn at random from srand(GetTickCount()) at SAUNA's start (0
# here), so the moves are `tools/sauna_plan.py` (it probes the port): 52
# arrows, most pressed 10 ms after Pacman steps onto a junction so he turns
# without stopping, and 3 left clicks that stop him on a junction. The
# last peanut goes at 21400: won, 9600 + 1000, in both versions (Pacman
# never meets a ghost, so the P-bugs only change pictures: P4 after each
# cork, P5 on each click).
#
# The `--fix all,-sauna_arcade_rules,-sauna_controls_screen` run is the bug fixes on the
# 1995 rules; the Corrigida's arcade game has its own scripts, sauna-corrigida-*.
#
#   zig-out/bin/noite --minigame sauna --headless --ms 22500 --input tools/play/sauna-alone-win.input
#   zig-out/bin/noite --minigame sauna --headless --ms 22500 --fix all,-sauna_arcade_rules,-sauna_controls_screen --input tools/play/sauna-alone-win.input
